  message: "Identity triage 2026-07-15: shape_id-coverage prerequisite for WI-vogij (clone/refactoring-lead feature). Re-run: csharp 16/16, solidity 11/11, wgsl 6/6 shape_id=null (100%) — analyze()-override bypasses the base stamp loop (base.py:3226-3232); wgsl hardcodes shape_id=None. A clone detector needs these populated."  # e050
- op: discuss  # 1a0f
  at: '2026-07-17T09:34:35Z'  # 1a0f
  by: agent  # 1a0f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a0f
  clock: 6  # 1a0f
  nonce: 1a0f  # 1a0f
  message: "CSHARP FACET DONE (PR #704, dev 58dd893b00). CSharpAnalyzer.analyze() now stamps shape_id from its populated node_for_symbol via a new _stamp_shape_ids helper; live: sherpa-csharp 0/105 -> 105/105 body-bearing symbols populated (class/method/struct/constructor), 105 csharp tests pass, csharp.py 100% cov. Surfaced + validated by the 2026-07-17 DEEP-cohort parity check. REMAINING (item stays open, scoped to these): (1) wgsl.py hardcodes shape_id=None at 3 construction sites (238/270/329); (2) solidity.py (analyze_solidity) emits no shape_id — BOTH are function-registered analyzers (not TreeSitterAnalyzer subclasses), so they can't call self.compute_shape_id; the fix needs the TreeSitterAnalyzer.compute_shape_id/_cst_structure logic extracted to a module-level callable (base.py, CORE) with byte-identical output verified (no shape_id churn on other langs). Distinct, larger refactor than the csharp class-based facet."  # 1a0f
- op: discuss  # 272c
  at: '2026-07-18T00:51:13Z'  # 272c
  by: agent  # 272c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 272c
  clock: 7  # 272c
  nonce: 272c  # 272c
  message: "Fix-shape premise CORRECTION (3-lens investigation 2026-07-17). The 2026-07-17 note claims wgsl/solidity 'are function-registered analyzers (not TreeSitterAnalyzer subclasses), so they can't call self.compute_shape_id' and concludes the fix needs compute_shape_id/_cst_structure extracted to a module-level base.py (CORE) callable with byte-identical verification. That premise is FALSE: wgsl.py:401 'class WgslAnalyzer(TreeSitterAnalyzer)' and solidity.py:753 'class SolidityAnalyzer(TreeSitterAnalyzer)' ARE subclasses; NEITHER overrides analyze(); the base analyze() auto-stamp loop (base.py:3277-3286) already runs for them — they just never populate analysis.node_for_symbol, so the loop finds nothing to stamp. The tree-sitter CST node is in scope at both construction sites. CORRECT minimal fix (NO base.py/CORE change, NO shape_id churn on other langs): populate node_for_symbol in the two extraction helpers — solidity: one line (analysis.node_for_symbol[symbol.id]=node where add_symbol has node in scope); wgsl: thread analysis.node_for_symbol into _extract_wgsl_symbols and set it at the function site (~wgsl.py:213/224). csharp was the HARD case (it DOES override analyze(), needing the _stamp_shape_ids replay PR #704 added); wgsl/solidity are the EASY case. Blast radius: 2 leaf analyzer files, zero base.py. LIVE IMPACT confirmed: repeat-finder (cli.py:6238 'if not shape_id or not language: continue') silently drops wgsl/solidity functions from clone detection (both in _CLONE_KINDS) — same hole PR #704 closed for csharp; WI-lutob isbefore WI-vogij. Stays coverage-completeness work (spec §6 'without' buckets); INV-jahiv flipped satisfied independently (shape_id is spec-optional coverage-scoped, not a uniform-contract parity field)."  # 272c
