  message: "Closed done — all 3 facets resolved (csharp PR #704; solidity+wgsl PR merged 7a2efee53f). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the item's own filed repro): fresh 'hypergumbo survey' on a /tmp wgsl+solidity repo — wgsl 3/3 body-bearing (struct + 2 functions) and solidity 2/2 (contract + function) now populate shape_id (was 100% null; the filed repro read 'csharp 16/16, solidity 11/11, wgsl 6/6 shape_id=null'). Production-path regression tests added in-package: test_wgsl_analyzer.py::{test_functions_carry_shape_id,test_structs_carry_shape_id}, test_solidity.py::test_body_bearing_symbols_carry_shape_id. ROOT CAUSE + FIX: wgsl/solidity never populated FileAnalysis.node_for_symbol, so the base-class auto-stamp loop (base.py:3277-3286) had nothing to stamp. Correcting the filed premise: both ARE TreeSitterAnalyzer subclasses that do NOT override analyze() (not 'function-registered analyzers needing a shared helper'), so populating node_for_symbol at the construction sites (solidity add_symbol = 1 line; wgsl _extract_wgsl_symbols function+struct sites) is all that was needed — NO base.py/CORE change, NO shape_id churn on other languages. Completes repeat-finder's structural-clone reach across C#/Solidity/WGSL (the cli.py:6238 shape_id-None drop no longer silently excludes them); unblocks WI-vogij coverage for these langs."  # d58a
